    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nHey, first things first, thanks for a great plugin!\r\n\r\nI'm having a strange issue with `yi'` operation while `mini.ai` is enabled.\r\n\r\nThe following error is reported:\r\n```\r\n07:13:40 msg_show.lua_error E5107: Error loading lua [string \":lua\"]:1: ')' expected near '', { search_method = ''\r\n07:13:40 msg_show cannot set clipboard contents\r\n07:13:40 msg_show stack traceback:\r\n07:13:40 msg_show ^I[C]: in function 'rpcrequest'\r\n07:13:40 msg_show ^I[string \"<nvim>\"]:31: in function <[string \"<nvim>\"]:30>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI've looked through `mini.ai` code and it seems it's being produced here:\r\n```lua\r\n  return '<Cmd>lua '\r\n    .. string.format(\r\n      [[MiniAi.select_textobject('%s', '%s', { search_method = '%s', n_times = %d, reference_region = %s, operator_pending = %s, vis_mode = %s })]],\r\n      ai_type,\r\n      vim.fn.escape(tobj_id, \"'\\\\\"),\r\n      opts.search_method,\r\n      vim.v.count1,\r\n      reference_region_field,\r\n      operator_pending_field,\r\n      vis_mode_field\r\n    )\r\n    .. '<CR>'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThough I'm not sure what to think of it. This particular part of `mini.ai` hasn't changed for a while and I've been having this issue with `yi'` only for a week or so. I'm not that well versed in Lua, so I'm not really sure what to think of it, apart from the hunch it's something about `'` being unescaped somewhere or my nvim setup playing tricks on me.\r\n\r\nCan you help me out with some tips what might be wrong on my end?\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu any_file_with_single_quotes`\r\n2. move cursor within any text, surrounded by `''`\r\n3. press `yi'`\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nText within `''` would be yanked\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nAn error happened instead",
