        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am also clueless as to why this can happen. Judging by the nature of the error, it seems to happen only with `'` textobject (and possible `\\`), right?\r\n\r\nOne thing I can suggest is, could you please try replacing `vim.fn.escape(tobj_id, \"'\\\\\")` argument (i.e. [this one](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c8bc67a35e627908da644c5f8cd26b3f987f2627/lua/mini/ai.lua#L1258)) with `vim.inspect(tobj_id)`? And see if you can reproduce the issue. The latter is a better solution in this type of situation, so replacing it should be a good idea anyway.\r\n\r\nAlso, judging by the log messages, I'd assume you run Neovim not directly from terminal emulator (more like Neovide or VS Code emulation). Is it correct?",
