        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski hey, thanks for checking it out! it actually does solve it, replacing `escape` with `vim.inspect` and replacing placeholder for tobj `'%s'` with just `%s`\r\n\r\nit now looks like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n  return '<Cmd>lua '\r\n    .. string.format(\r\n      [[MiniAi.select_textobject('%s', %s, { search_method = '%s', n_times = %d, reference_region = %s, operator_pending = %s, vis_mode = %s })]],\r\n      ai_type,\r\n      vim.inspect(tobj_id),\r\n      opts.search_method,\r\n      vim.v.count1,\r\n      reference_region_field,\r\n      operator_pending_field,\r\n      vis_mode_field\r\n    )\r\n    .. '<CR>'\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nyep, I'm running with Neovide and lazyvim, though tried directly in the terminal, was getting the same error, but not yet tried on a bare nvim with `mini.ai` only.\r\n\r\nI'm sure it has nothing to do with `mini.ai`, judging from the error itself - it would be somewhat related to neovim or lua handling/adapter, but that sounds a bit stupid, since I haven't updated it in a while and a bug of that magnitude will be all over the place by now, in every bugtracker, and I've looked somewhat thoroughly before posting here.\r\n\r\nIf you're interested in trying to figure it out - I can always debug on my side, since it's reproducing here, but I'm not sure if you'd want to spend time on that, since there's no reports of this. I can make pull request out of this, but, again, I'm not sure if it's relevant or you want that, considering it's only me having an issue",
