            "body": "The `vim.inspect()` usage instead of `vim.fn.escape()` should now be part of `main` branch and (hopefully) fixing the issue.\r\n\r\n> If you're interested in trying to figure it out - I can always debug on my side, since it's reproducing here, but I'm not sure if you'd want to spend time on that, since there's no reports of this. I can make pull request out of this, but, again, I'm not sure if it's relevant or you want that, considering it's only me having an issue\r\n\r\nUsing the `vim.inspect()` is the better approach here, so probably not worth going fully down the rabbit hole here.\r\n\r\nOne thing I am curious though, what OS are you using? Is it Windows, by any chance?",
