            "body": "> and an answer to that is, probably, why it would be a huge waste of time =) speaking about rabbit holes - it's mandatory for me to use windows for one of the projects I'm working on, so my current setup for neovim is:\r\n\r\nI see. My impression here is that there is an issue somewhere in the Neovide or Neovim which results into `vim.fn.escape()` misbehaving inside RPC calls (remote calls with which Neovide \"talks\" to Neovim) on Windows. Maybe even with this particular `vim.fn.escape('string', \"'\\\\\")` call (as it involves backward slash which might be an issue on Windows). Probably in on itself worth investigating, but not sure how invested you can allow yourself to be here.",
