        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski well, yeah, I've figured it out\r\n\r\nletting you know just for the giggles, an old as the world itself story of \"stupidity strikes back\". I've messed up my `cpoptions` somewhere around last week. to the point that it landed to have `n` flag only (and the default is `aABceFs_`)\r\n\r\nsooo, probably it's missing `B` flag that messed things up for me beyond repair, which prevents `\\` to be treated as `Ctrl-V` in mappings, commands, abbreviations\r\n\r\nspent half a day and only found out during a full directory diff of two nvim configs (nice job, man, nice jooob)\r\n\r\nsorry for spending your time on this, big thanks for looking into it and making a fix =)",
